$DIR/main.p:31:2: cannot store v.Slice() in package variable keepInts, which outlives v
    v.Slice() points into v. v is a local variable of storeLocal (declared at
    main.p:29). When storeLocal returns, v's memory is reclaimed, but package
    variables live for the whole program, so package variable keepInts would be
    left pointing at reclaimed memory.
    Go would move this memory to the heap, and its garbage collector would free
    it later. Plutonium has no garbage collector and never moves memory to the
    heap behind the program's back, so that every allocation is visible in the
    code.
    Store values instead of views of v, or allocate v and store its owner, an
    owned[pluto/vec.Vec[int]], which moves there:
        keepInts = new(pluto/vec.Vec[int])
    (see "Views" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.3)
    (run "pluto explain E3002" for a longer explanation)

$DIR/main.p:42:9: cannot return b.Items(), which points into b, a local variable of throughMethod
    b.Items() points into b. b is a local variable of throughMethod (declared at
